**Definition 22.3 (total rational block-image recognition).** For any
finite candidate term and rational coordinate list, first require
canonical finite encoding, reachable syntax, exact material support,
nonzero field and all coordinates in $[0,1]$. At each non-alpha stage,
start its gap counter at zero. While all coordinates are positive,
apply its exact rational inverse $T^{-1}$, increment the counter and
reject any negative, greater-than-one or wholly zero field.

At the first zero require that the positive support is a nonempty
rooted prefix-closed support $V_s$ parsing to some $s\in\mathcal D$.
Require that comparison with the entire current term has exactly the
possibilities in Theorem 22.2, with at least one changed old leaf.
No old branch is changed except through those recursive comparisons;
each changed old leaf is edited once. Require positive retained
coordinates. After the outermost successful collapse, each further
non-alpha stage must have counter at least one. Restrict and continue.
At alpha require a scalar in $(0,1]$ and double until reaching or
exceeding one; accept only equality. Return its block/gap certificate.

